      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Because of its side-effects, long-term administration of ticlopidine limits the use of the sirolimus-eluting stent (SES) in Japan."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "METHODS AND RESULTS",
          "content": "Side-effects of ticlopidine occurred in 41 (9.3%) of 440 patients who underwent SES implantation. The majority were liver dysfunction (4.5%) and rash (3.6%). One patient died from severe liver dysfunction. Neutropenia occurred in 3 patients (0.7%). It is remarkable that 28% of side-effects occurred >8 weeks after the initiation of ticlopidine."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Ticlopidine has a relative high rate of side-effects. Clopidogrel should be approved for prevention of stent thrombosis as soon as possible."
        }
      ]},
